{"text": "PARADISE\nRIDGE\n\nFinished Wine\nSyrah 82% Grenache 18%\n\nAppellation\n\nRussian River Valley\n\nVinyard\n\nEstate \u2018Hoenselaars\u2019 Vineyard\n\nAlcohol\n13.1%\n\nTitratable Acidity\n7.0 grams/liter\n\npH\n3.19\n\nResidual Sugar\nfe)\n\nSuggested Retail\n$22\n\nPARADISE\nRIDGE\n\n2020 'Pretty and Pink' Ros\u00e9\nRussian River Valley\n\nVineyard Notes\n\nThe 1.8-acre \u2018Hoenselaars\u2019 Vineyard was planted in 2002 facing West on a cordon\npruned trellis system. The Syrah, Estrella clone, came from Rhone, France via Paso\nRobles. Grenache's origin is believed to have come from Spain, but has been widely\nplanted in the Rhone region and Southern France for centuries. These grapes are\ngrown a little differently than if they were destined to be red wine. At pruning, we leave\nmore buds (more fruit) per vine which slows the ripening process down along with\npreserving more of the fruit's natural acidity. The canopy is managed so the majority of\n\nthe clusters are more shaded, capturing the more delicate characters in the fruit\n\nWinemaker Notes\n\nWe made this Ros\u00e9 in the traditional style, starting with an early morning hand harvest\nThe fruit is whole-cluster pressed to tank, where the juice is kept at 40\u00b0F for 10 days; the\ntank is mixed daily with dry ice in a process known as \u2018Stabulation\u2019, which originates\nfrom Provence, France. This increases the thiol aroma molecules in the juice which are\nthe pre- cursers to many of the wine's aromas and flavor. The juice was then lightly\nfined, settled, and racked to stainless steel where an unusually cool (50\u00b0F) fermentation\nlasting several weeks utilized a combination of native and selected yeasts, to increase\nboth texture and complexity. This is a single fermentation wine. Maturation is 100%\n\nstainless steel with no malolactic fermentation.\n\nTasting Notes\n\nThis classic Ros\u00e9 delivers everything that we could hope for. Pretty aromas of soft red\nfruit, white peach, along with spring blossoms are supported by a core of minerality on\nthe nose. The entry is vibrant and clean, echoing the wine's aroma. A curiously rich\n\nmouthfeel is both persistent and refreshing leading to a finish that leaves you craving for\n\nx\n\nPARADISE\nRIDGE\n4545 Thomas Lake Harris Drive, Santa Rosa CA 95403\n707.528.9463 | info@prwinery.com | prwinery.com | @paradiseridge\n\nmore.",
